# Living Docs (published projects)

When a change affects domain language, architecture, or user-visible
capabilities in a **published** project tree, follow the three-phase workflow
in [living-docs](../skills/developer/references/living-docs.md).

Quick order:

1. **Phase 1 (before code in the source repo):** `Glossary.md` →
   `C4-Code-Domain-Model.puml`
2. **Phase 2:** implement in the project repo (out of meta whitelist)
3. **Phase 3 (sync to meta):** structural C4, Dynamic diagrams, deployment,
   User Story Map + epics

Sync Phase 1–3 doc updates into this meta-repo via stacked Draft PRs
([delivery-github-stack](../skills/developer/references/delivery-github-stack.md)).

C4 naming and visual tracks: [c4-model](../skills/developer/references/c4-model.md).
